From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: computerguy526 <355510486+computerguy526@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:46:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: prepfast, opt-in prepare speedups (flush export,
 collect-only, stable keys, segment pre-fault)

Every piece is off unless its variable is set; with none set the driver behaves as before.
- nps5_kk_archive_flush(wait_ms): exported; writes the pending archive segment (compact mode: the one compacted
  segment) and returns, so a prepare no longer sleeps a fixed flush period before _Exit.
- KK_MSL_COLLECT_ONLY=1: a library without a metallib is only collected (MSL written), not compiled; applies once the
  device's own libraries exist (mtl_compiler_collect_only_arm); the compute "seen" log still runs.
- KK_ARCHIVE_STAMP_EPOCH=<n> / KK_LIBKEY_CONTENT=1: archive store stamp keyed on a hand-bumped epoch + OS build + GPU,
  metallib key on MSL text + options + OS major + GPU, so a KK commit that changes neither keeps both stores.
- KK_PIPELINE_ARCHIVE_PREFAULT=1: every segment's absent pages are read in by all cores before the archives are opened.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
